				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-pighead" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3242824); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3242824&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608130608" alt="The Pighead" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3242824)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-pighead" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3242824); return false;" >The Pighead</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607888826 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Dec 2020 19:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843988">
									

<p>Have been summoned by PM, so here I come. Pighead In, here's a short review of your draft.</p>
<p>So, this is pretty good when it comes to the writing, but I have two issues with it. The first, the main one, is the fact that for me, the end is really abrupt. The entire thing is pretty short and when I came to the end of the interview, I was like &quot;That's all?&quot;. I felt like there were more things that you could tell, about why SCP XXX-1 wants to find love, about the feelings of isolation it could have (and who were really briefly touched upon on the very last sentence).</p>
<p>And the second thing is that at this moment, for me, this draft is &quot;Mermaid, but SCP&quot;. Like, I feel like I just see a mermaid who is adapted into an SCP. And not that I'm against mythological creatures being turned into SCPs, the history of the site had proved that it could work really efficiently. But with the really short draft, that creates a situation when it's not really interesting to see this, it's like &quot;So, here's this mythological creature and its abilities and nothing else&quot;.</p>
<p>What I can suggest to you is to dig deeper into how the mermaids live as a society, what are their collective purpose in life and what is the backstory of SCP-XXXX-1, what are the events who led it to wanting a mate, a person to love, what led it to wanting not just having intercourse, but having a person for spending the rest of its life with. With that, you have the potential to tell a pretty good story about how isolation and being tired of just doing what you have to do can led you to wanting something new in life and experiencing, for the first time, human feelings.</p>
<p>So, think about all that, for the rest, your writing has potential. It's all for me, Pighead Out.</p>

							</div>

								
					
